\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {6}Work-item lifecycle and stopping conditions}{9}{section.6}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Work-item lifecycle and stopping conditions.} Each work item passes authority and contract checks, evidence assembly and classification, bounded drafting, deterministic verification, semantic verification and a named human review gate before a signed handoff package is produced. Numbered stops correspond to the seven stopping conditions in the main text. Rejection, revision, escalation and expiry are first-class outcomes. In a stopped state the assistant may summarize the issue and name the responsible role, and it cannot infer approval, legal basis, risk acceptance, data quality or a site attestation. Re-entry requires new authority or corrected evidence.}}{9}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
